1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He is '''not''' given the surname Rappaport in 1) Otser HaRabanim # 4546, '''nor''' in 2) Unbroken Chain, 3rd Ed, V1, p706, G8, '''nor''' in 3) Jacobi Papers V2, p6, 10.1, nor in 4) Pinkhes Kehillot Polyn. In some 
2 CONC sources it is his son Yitzach Avraham Katz (https://www.geni.com/people/%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%99-%D7%99%D7%A6%D7%97%D7%A7-%D7%90%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%94%D7%9D-%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%99-%D7%94%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%9F-%D7%9B-%D7%A5-%D7%90%D7%91-%D7%93
2 CONC -%D7%A4%D7%99%D7%A0%D7%98%D7%A9%D7%95%D7%91-%D7%9E%D7%97-%D7%A1-%D7%A9%D7%95-%D7%AA-%D7%9B%D7%AA%D7%A8-%D7%9B%D7%94%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%94/6000000000961693663) who is the first to be associated with the Rappaport surname and in others 
2 CONC it is the latter's brother, Yitzach 'Keter Kahuna' (https://www.geni.com/people/R-Yitzchok-Katz-AB-D-Pintchuv/6000000211576548856) who is the first to be associated with the Rappaport surname. Pinkhes Kehill Polyn calls "Keter Kah
2 CONC una' as a Rapaport, but not the brother nor the father. Unbroken Chain calls both brothers Rapaports but not their father. Otser HaRabnim calls neither of the two brothers nor their father as Rapaports (# 1223, # 10727 and # 4546)
2 CONC . So there are two possibilities on the able as to which of these brothers is the one who brought the Rappaport surname into the Katz HaCohen family, and based on Pinkhes Kehilot Poyln it seems to be 'Keter Kahuna', which implies 
2 CONC that the spouse of Keter Kahuna is from the Rapaport line (see her father's profile for possible connection to the Rapaport line: https://www.geni.com/people/R-Isaac-of-Josefow/6000000007319877332) . (05 SEP 2025) 
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
