1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1748 lived Nathan FRIEDLANDT in Godene Gassen Prague with his father Löb, a draper (Tuch) and two unmarried sisters Freidl and Hanele and one married Lea . (Sworn Declarations of Prague Jewish Families 1748-1749
2 CONC  (1751) Edition of a source on the return of Jews expelled by Maria Theresia, No 900, page 154-155)
2 CONT
2 CONT He died before 1793, then his wife Rössl lived in Prague as a widow (Soupis zidovskych rodin v Cechach z roku 1793. vol VI/1, page 56)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record:
