1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~prohel/names/misc/porges.html#le
2 CONT
2 CONT From A Memoir by Erika Schulhof Rybek. "On My Own. Decoding the Conspiracy of Silence". Moses Porges and Leopold Juda Porges introduced to Prague the city's first steam engine around 1808 to run a calico or cotton printing plant. 
2 CONC It is apparently recorded that Emperor Ferdinand I, who was promoting modernization, offered the brothers what they wished and when they requested equality for the Jews, they were told they asked too much but were granted full cit
2 CONC izens rights on 6/5/1841 and the hereditary title of Edle von Portheim. Apparently Portheim was based on the Porges famiy origins in Porto, Portugal.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>see also Villa Portheimka in Prague 5 - Smíchov, Štefánikova street No.68/12 (in Czech)<br/>
2 CONT https://cs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portheimka
