1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1811 https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CS8P-2GZF?i=411&cat=2826844
2 CONT
2 CONT 1816 https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSFR-29TS-J?i=548
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT New evidence makes it clear that the father of Avraham Yakov is not Shmuel b. Noda B'Yehuda, but rather Shmuel b. Chaim: in the 1813 Family List of Vilna there is a Landau family consisting of a Samuel b. Chaim, married to a Roche
2 CONC l b. Chaim, with a son Icko age 11, a son Leyzer age 7, a daughter Freda newborn, and a daughter Gitta newborn, and also a family consisting of a Jankiel Abram age 19, son of Samuel, husband of Hana, daughter of Hirsh, parents of 
2 CONC Chaim newborn. The 1816 Family List shows that two daughters were added to the family Jankiel b Chaim and Rokhl b. Chaim (both parents have a father named Chaim on both the 1813 and the 1816 Family List). Jankiel had already moved
2 CONC  out of the father's household and started a family by the time of the 1813 Family List.
2 CONT
2 CONT This alters some of the prior source information, which I post below for the record:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) in Unbroken Chain 3rd Ed Volume 3 p 765 12.1, the spouse of Avraham Yakov b. Shmuel HaLevi b Noda B'Yehuda HaLevi  is given as "Hanale Rechlis daughter of Zvi Hersh of Vilna (see Chapter VII Elias Family)"; upon reviewing the E
2 CONC lias Family in Chapter VII, I see that Zvi Hersh of Vilna is Zvi Hersh Elias (Vol 3, p. 169, 10.2 and that he has a daughter "Hanale Rechel's" who marries Avraham Yakov b. Shmuel HaLevi b. Noda B'Yehuda HaLevi (Vol 3, p. 171, 11.4
2 CONC ),
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) then in Jacobi Papers Volume 4, p 445, 7.4m, Rechel Volozhiner is said to have married "R. Schmuel VII (b.) Abraham VIII (non-levitic) Schatellis-"Landau" " [this seems to be Shmuel son of Yakov Avraham, born slightly after the
2 CONC  1813 Family List]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) in Unbroken Chain 3rd Ed Volume 2 p 313 13.2, Zvi Hirsch Simchovitz is said to be the "son in law of R. Samuel Landau of Vilna, son in law of R. Haim Landau of Podkamien (first cousin of the Noda B'Yehuda...)"  
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) in Otser HaRabanim # 19240 Shmuel Landau of Vilna, whose father is not given, is said to be the son in law of Chaim Segal Landau # 6054, who is a 1st cousin of Noda B'Yehuda
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems pretty clear from the Vilna Family List that Avraham Yakov, husband of Hanale daughter of Tsvi Hereh of Vilna is not the son of Samuel b Noda B'Yehuda, but rather the son of Samuel b. Chaim, who is in turn the son in law 
2 CONC of Chaim HaLevi Landau (a 1st cousin of Noda B;Yehuda).
2 CONT
2 CONT For these reasons I am disconnecting Abraham Yakov from Shmuel b. Noda B'Yehuda (https://www.geni.com/people/R-Samuel-HaLevi-Landau-ABD-Prague/5356338671200088466)
