1 NAME Ascher Lemuel "Lamle" /Lehmann/
2 GIVN Ascher Lemuel "Lamle"
2 SURN Lehmann
2 _MARNM Lehmann
2 NICK Ascher Laemle Weldt
2 NICK Ascher Lemuel Weldtsberg
2 NICK Ascher Lemmle Weldtsberg
2 NICK Weltdsberg
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 JUN 1769
2 PLAC oberfränkischen Landgemeinde Zeckendorf
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 APR 1858
2 ADDR
3 CITY Verden
3 STAE Lower Saxony
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU kleiner Händler
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marcus Lehmanns Vater, Ascher Laemle Weldt, genannt Lehmann (1769-1858), stammte aus der oberfränkischen Landgemeinde Zeckendorf. Er folgte einem seiner Brüder nach Böhmen. Als er zur österreichischen Armee eingezo
2 CONC gen werden sollte, floh er nach Norddeutschland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Er war neben seinem Beruf als kleiner Händler, den er mit wechselndem Erfolg ausübte, auch rabbinischer Gelehrter. Er hatte an der Prager Jeschiwa (Talmud-Hochschule, ähnlich der Halberstädter Klaus) noch ein rein jüdisches Studiu
2 CONC m absolviert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Medaon", Berndt Strobach
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT R' Marcus (Meir) Lehmann was his youngest of eight children.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://digital.cjh.org:80/R/-?func=dbin-jump-full&amp;object_id=637688&amp;silo_library=GEN01
2 CONT
2 CONT Object		 	- Complex Object ()
2 CONT
2 CONT Title	Urgrossvaters Tagebuch, 1786-1850
2 CONT
2 CONT Access Restrictions	Memoir is digitized.
2 CONT
2 CONT Creator or Author	Weldtsberg, Ascher Laemle .
2 CONT
2 CONT Creator or Author	Lehmann, Max .
2 CONT
2 CONT Creator or Author	Lehmann, Martin .
2 CONT
2 CONT Date	Verden,, 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT LC Subject	Rabbis. Orthodox Judaism -- Publications -- Periodicals. Education, Higher -- 1786-1789 Napoleonic Wars, 1800-1815 Editors Merchants
2 CONT
2 CONT Subject	Mendershausen family
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes	
2 CONT
2 CONT Ascher Laemle Weldtsberg (called Lehmann) was born in Zeckendorf (Upper Franconia) in 1769. He studied at the Yeshiva in Prague between 1786 and 1789. He settled in Verden (Aller) and adopted the name Weldtsberg. He died there in 
2 CONC 1858. His son Markus Lehmann was the founder and editor of the orthodox periodical "Israelit", and a rabbi in Mainz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Exact description of author's journey through Bohemia to take up his studies at the Yeshiva in Prague in 1786; return to Germany; army supplier in Napoleonic Wars; as merchant in Verden (Aller); contains genealogical information o
2 CONC n Lehmann, Leeser, Mendel, Friedlaender, Prins, Phillips, Mendershausen, Tscherniak, Hertz and Preuss families.
2 CONT
2 CONT Publisher	Lehmann, Max
2 CONT
2 CONT Publisher	Lehmann, Martin
2 CONT
2 CONT Object Type	Memoirs and biographies
2 CONT
2 CONT Extent	67 + 59 pages.
2 CONT
2 CONT Call Number	ME 682 Call Number	MM 80
2 CONT
2 CONT Citation Link	http://digital.cjh.org:80/R/-?func=dbin-jump-full&amp;object_id=637688&amp;silo_library=GEN01
2 CONT
2 CONT Language	German
2 CONT
2 CONT Language	English
2 CONT
2 CONT Repository	Leo Baeck Institute, LBI Archives, 15 West 16th Street, New York, NY 10011
2 CONT
2 CONT Record ID	637688
2 CONT
