1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 MAR 1819
2 ADDR
3 CITY Berlin
3 STAE Berlin
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was born on January 10th, 1758 in Berlin and died there on March 20th, 1819. His parents were the merchant Bendix Samuel (1734-1817) and Sara, née Rieß (* after 1730-1815), he had at least to brothers (as mentio
2 CONC ned above). On January 6th, 1790, he married Channa/Hanna Aron (1769-1823), they had at least three sons, as mentioned above. Samuel Bentheim (until 1812, his name was Samuel Bendix) was a merchant and became a Berlin citizen on A
2 CONC pril 6th, 1809 (before 1809, Jews were denied this status). He lived at Königstraße 10 in 1809 and at Spandauer Straße 30, corner of Königstraße in 1818, shortly before his death. This all in the city centre, close to today’s rail
2 CONC way station Alexanderplatz (maybe you know Berlin a bit).
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 28th, 1807 he became a member of the Gesellschaft der Freunde and got the membership number A 172. He was not able to enter the society earlier because when the Gesellschaft was founded in 1792, it decided that only ba
2 CONC chelors were allowed to become members. This rule was abandoned in 1807, and Samuel Bendix (later Bentheim) applied for membership immediately. – In 1812, Bentheim together with other members of the Gesellschaft der Freunde decide
2 CONC d to found a new society, the “Gesellschaft zur Beförderung der Industrie unter den Bewohnern der Königl. Preußischen Staaten jüdischer Religion” (Society for the support of handicraft among the Jewish residents in the royal Pruss
2 CONC ian states). The society aimed at broadening the spectrum of professions of Prussian Jews who until then usually chose to become merchants (mainly because before 1812 most other professions were not allowed to them.) Bentheim beca
2 CONC me one of the members of the board of this society.'
