2 CONC  original record books or in the data entry process. This is true for the record numbers as well as the index entry for databases that were generated from the indices in the record books rather than the records themselves. As alwa
2 CONC ys, it is prudent for the researcher, when using secondary source data such as this work, to examine the primary source data for verification. It is always best for the genealogist to view the actual records pertaining to his/her 
2 CONC family to verify the interpretation, and glean additional facts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additionally, since spelling was irrelevant in the 19th century Kingdom of Poland records, some potential matches will not be found even with Daitch-Mokotoff soundex techniques. 
