1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rebbe Yosef Friedman of Rimanov was the only son of Rebbe Tzvi Hirsch of Rimanov. He was orphaned of his father at the age of three. His mother Malka became remarried to [https://www.geni.com/people/R-Israel-Friedm
2 CONC an-Founder-of-the-Ruzhiner-Dynasty/6000000000644946559 Rebbe Yisrael of Ruzhin] who raised him. After R' Yisrael's death his son R' Avraham Yaakov of Sadiger continued to look after R. Yosef, who adopted his stepfather's surname "
2 CONC Friedman" in gratitude. In 1867 R' Yosef finally succeeded his father R' Tzvi Hirsch and became the third Rebbe of Rimanov. During the Shemitta controversy of 1888 R' Yosef joined the other Chassidic leaders who opposed the Heter 
2 CONC Mechira. In 1896, R' Yosef resigned as the Rimanover Rebbe and was succeeded by his son-in-law Rebbe Asher Yeshayahu. Rebbe Yosef passed away on the 24th of Nissan, 1914.  
