0 @I6000000028618784638@ INDI
1 NAME Leopold /Schuster/
2 GIVN Leopold
2 SURN Schuster
2 _MARNM Schuster
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1791
2 ADDR
3 CITY Frankfurt Am Main
3 STAE Hessen
3 CTRY Prussia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 FEB 1871
2 PLAC 11 Upper Belgrave St.
2 ADDR
3 ADR3 Belgrave Sq.
3 CITY London
3 POST SW1
3 CTRY Great Britain
1 OCCU cotton trader; merchant banker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Brief Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Schuster
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Leopold Schuster''' (1791 – 27 February 1871)was a German-born British cotton trader turned merchant banker, best known as the Chairman of the London and Brighton Railway and then the London, Brighton and South Coast Railway, a
2 CONC nd part of the consortia which bought The Crystal Palace.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of a cotton merchant, he moved to England in 1808, and in 1820 formed the trading company Leo Schuster, Brothers & Co., cotton merchants based in Manchester, Bradford and Liverpool.  Like many German Jews in Northwest Engl
2 CONC and at the time, he converted to Unitarianism.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his first wife, Emilie, he had a son and a daughter. His elder son Samuel Leo Schuster (11 May 1830 – 23 December 1884)[6] married the eldest daughter of the 5th Earl of Orkney, while his daughter Mariana Emily Schuster married
2 CONC  baronet Sir William Dickason Clay and after Clay's death married senior civil servant Arthur Haliburton, 1st Baron Haliburton.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his second marriage to Mary Howard in 1845 he had two more daughters and a second son, Leo Francis Howard Schuster (1852-1927), a music-lover and patron of the arts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also the uncle of Sir Felix Schuster, banker and financier, and Sir Francis Schuster.
2 CONT
2 CONT On his death, his estate was valued at over £500,000, making him one of the most successful merchants of his time.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p3858.htm#i38578
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo Schuster lived at Roehampton, Surrey, EnglandG.2
2 CONT Children of Leo Schuster
2 CONT
2 CONT #Samuel Leo Schuster+2 d. 1884
2 CONT #Amy Schuster+2 d. 31 Jan 1915
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Schuster Leo Schuster]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. --------------------
